<title>USA: Allegiance shares climb on Q4 write-down.</title>
<headline>Allegiance shares climb on Q4 write-down.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Allegiance Corp climbed 1-1/8 to 19-7/8 after it announced a non-cash $550 million, fourth-quarter charge on a writedown of goodwill left after its spinoff by Baxter International Inc.</p>
<p>Although the charge will cause the hospital products supplier to report a loss for the fourth quarter and 1996, the writedown will boost net income on an ongoing basis by reducing amortization costs, the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a mild positive. It's a non-cash charge. Everyone knew it was coming,&quot; said Merrill Lynch analyst Oliver Moses.</p>
<p>Allegiance began trading independently October 1.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
